Audio Share Rust
Copyright 2024-2026 Audio Share Rust contributors

This project is a from-scratch Rust re-creation of mkckr0/audio-share
(https://github.com/mkckr0/audio-share), Copyright 2022-2024 mkckr0,
licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0. Its protocol design
(TCP control + UDP PCM data, heartbeat keep-alives), the Linux virtual
sink configuration documented in the README, and the Android feature set
(quick-settings tile, loudness boost) inspired this implementation.

The wire protocol used here ("ASR2", version 2) is a new, self-describing
framing and is NOT compatible with the original project's protobuf-based
protocol; original Android builds cannot connect to this server and vice
versa.

This product includes software developed as part of the Rust project and
the following notable dependencies (all under MIT/Apache-2.0-compatible
licenses):
- tokio (MIT), cpal (Apache-2.0), wasapi-rs (MIT), mdns-sd (MIT),
  if-addrs (MIT/Apache-2.0), clap (MIT/Apache-2.0), rubato-free custom
  linear resampler, Tauri (MIT/Apache-2.0), AndroidX / Compose (Apache-2.0).
